WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:20.283
Kara: Hi, Mark! Hi, Coby!

2
00:00:20.284 --> 00:00:23.227
Kara: Want to see my project again?

3
00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:25.537
It's about butterflies.

4
00:00:25.538 --> 00:00:32.541
Mark and Coby: No, thanks.

5
00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:35.151
Mark: Wow! Are those raisins?

6
00:00:35.152 --> 00:00:39.881
Juan: Yes. I mixed vinegar with baking soda to make them swim.

7
00:00:39.882 --> 00:00:42.773
Coby: Cool!

8
00:00:42.774 --> 00:00:47.211
Mrs. Conlan: Mark, the judges are going to your table.

9
00:00:47.212 --> 00:00:49.384
Mrs. Conlan: You'd better get over there.

10
00:00:49.385 --> 00:00:52.273
Mark: The best projects win ribbons.

11
00:00:52.274 --> 00:00:57.622
Mark: I hope I win one!

12
00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:00.944
Judge 1: What's your project, young man?

13
00:01:00.945 --> 00:01:03.604
Mark: I studied how plants grow.

14
00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.888
Mark: And I made a movie about it.

15
00:01:05.889 --> 00:01:08.356
Judge 2: You made a movie?

16
00:01:08.357 --> 00:01:10.805
May we see it?

17
00:01:10.806 --> 00:01:13.081
Mark: Sure!

18
00:01:13.082 --> 00:01:14.524
Judge 1: Hmm.

19
00:01:14.525 --> 00:01:16.396
Judge 2: Oh . . .

20
00:01:16.397 --> 00:01:23.499
Judge 1: Your project is very unusual. Thank you.

21
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.920
Zack: Now what?

22
00:01:25.921 --> 00:01:29.309
Mrs. Conlan: We have to wait for the judges to decide.

23
00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:34.567
Mr. Conlan: Mark, let me take another picture of you.

24
00:01:34.568 --> 00:01:40.962
Mr. Conlan: Stand right there, in front of your plant again!

25
00:01:40.963 --> 00:01:44.133
Mrs. Conlan: What are those?

26
00:01:44.134 --> 00:01:46.088
Mark: Tornados in a bottle.

27
00:01:46.089 --> 00:01:50.081
Mr. Conlan: I see they were popular this year.

28
00:01:50.082 --> 00:01:54.490
Mark: That's for sure.

29
00:01:54.491 --> 00:01:57.772
Mr. Miller: Thank you for coming to the science fair.

30
00:01:57.773 --> 00:02:00.868
Mr. Miller: We had some great projects this year.

31
00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:06.402
Mr. Miller: Soon we'll be giving out ribbons for the best ones.

32
00:02:06.403 --> 00:02:09.806
Mark: I hope mine wins.

33
00:02:09.807 --> 00:02:13.632
Mr. Miller: But first, we'd like to show you a project.

34
00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.290
Man: Show us? What is he talking about?

35
00:02:17.291 --> 00:02:27.422
Mr. Miller: Lights, please!

36
00:02:27.423 --> 00:02:39.736
Crowd: Amazing! Wow!

37
00:02:39.737 --> 00:02:42.411
Miss Gray: Nice job, Mark!

38
00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:44.201
You won a ribbon!

39
00:02:44.202 --> 00:02:46.147
Mark: Thanks, Miss Gray.

40
00:02:46.148 --> 00:02:49.736
Miss Gray: I just love science, don't you?

41
00:02:49.737 --> 00:02:52.708
Mark: Yes!
